Modifications
-------------
This fork was created from the httpSMS Android client. The following changes
have been made to the original work. Changes are ongoing — refer to the git
history for the full record.

Branding and configuration
  - Rebranded as "SMSGateway" (application id com.sevanam.androidsmsgateway).
    The original source namespace com.httpsms is still used by the code.
  - User interface rewritten and localised to Indonesian.
  - Forced light mode; removed the dark theme and its night resources.
  - Replaced the built-in server URL with a per-machine value read from
    local.properties.

Source layout
  - Moved the source tree into packages by concern: core/, data/ (api/, io/,
    model/), sms/, push/, background/, ui/, util/.
  - Split the previous monolithic models file and API service into
    single-purpose files.

Backend layer
  - Introduced a shared OkHttp client, a uniform result type, a central list
    of endpoint paths, a single traffic log and an error-body reader.
  - Request and response bodies are now serialised with Klaxon models instead
    of hand-built JSON strings.

Login and registration
  - Replaced the login credential with a one-time pairing code and a pairing
    call (POST gateway/pair) that carries the device's FCM token, replacing the
    previous per-SIM registration at login. Per-SIM FCM token registration is
    retained for token refresh, app upgrades and SIM changes.
  - Added an information sheet explaining that the active line is fixed until
    logout.

Messaging
  - Message status reports (SENT / DELIVERED / FAILED) now also send a device
    heartbeat.
  - Removed an experimental, unused WebSocket transport.

Setup and device requirements
  - Replaced the setup prompts with blocking dialogs for battery optimisation,
    SMS permission and OEM autostart, and added an information sheet for the
    SIM card field on the home screen.

